comments[7]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-08-29T05:26:08.328Z",pi-agent,"Rejected scalar values containing parser-active control characters after unescaping and added end-to-end regressions for escaped semicolon, ampersand, and pipe."
  "2026-08-29T05:33:01.677Z",pi-agent,"Follow-up Greptile round: assignment-only commands ending at && or || now remain persistent scalar bindings; added direct and end-to-end regressions for both list operators."
  "2026-08-29T05:39:55.818Z",pi-agent,"Second Greptile follow-up: parse assignment-only command sequences with multiple bindings and optional if/while/until condition prefixes; regressions cover multi-binding and if-condition publishes."
  "2026-08-29T05:46:26.918Z",pi-agent,"Third Greptile follow-up: discover assignment-only commands after then/do control-body boundaries while stripping shell comments quote-safely; added direct and end-to-end control-body regressions."
  "2026-08-29T05:52:58.495Z",pi-agent,"Fourth Greptile follow-up: split only top-level shell list operators while tracking quote, backtick, and parenthesis scope; nested quoted/substitution assignments no longer leak into the outer scalar map."
  "2026-08-29T05:58:53.158Z",pi-agent,"Fifth Greptile follow-up: include else and elif control prefixes in assignment-only segment recognition; direct and end-to-end regressions cover both."
  "2026-08-29T06:05:25.656Z",pi-agent,"Sixth Greptile follow-up: stopped projecting control-flow assignments into a file-wide map because execution is unknowable statically; unresolved publisher variables followed by publish now fail closed as foreign/unresolved publish paths."
